    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "log: escape C1 control characters in messages",
    "user": {
      "login": "fametrano",
      "id": 3296421,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY0MjE=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3296421?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fametrano",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The log escapes control characters so that a message cannot drive the terminal it is printed on, but it lets through the UTF-8 form of the C1 controls U+0080 to U+009F. VTE, the library behind GNOME Terminal and others, decodes these as CSI, OSC, DCS and the rest, like their `ESC [`, `ESC ]` and `ESC P` forms.\n\nI escape the two-byte sequences 0xC2 0x80 to 0xC2 0x9F as `\\xc2\\x9b` and so on. Since 0xC2 is never a continuation byte, this needs no UTF-8 decoder, and all other non-ASCII text still passes untouched, as asked in #17095 and #35833. Single bytes 0x80 to 0x9F stay as they are, since they occur inside valid UTF-8. The new cases in `test_LogEscapeMessage` fail on master and pass with the change.\n",
